<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Consultative Assembly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945–</span> · Also known as Majelis Permusyawaratan Rakyat, MPR</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) is the highest legislative body of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Under the 1945 constitution it was the supreme organ of state that elected the president and vice-president and set broad state policy, a role <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suharto">Suharto</a> used to secure re-election unopposed six times. Constitutional amendments of 1999–2002, which it passed itself, introduced direct presidential elections, and it now consists of the members of the House of Representatives and the Regional Representative Council.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-consultative-assembly.jpg" alt="People's Consultative Assembly" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Barkah Yusuf, Sameboat · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_People%27s_Consultative_Assembly_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
